  "title": "The Kit Inventory Finds an Empty Slot",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "public safety/preparedness",
  "premise": "A household wants its emergency supplies to match an official checklist, but sealed bags make missing categories invisible. A reviewed inventory illustration opens labeled slots and records what requires attention without inventing supply quantities.",
  "hook": "What is missing that a closed bag cannot show?",
  "visible_action": "A kit becomes a cutaway grid; checklist categories align with slots and missing entries become review flags.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Preparedness supplies benefit from an inventory matched to current official guidance and household needs.",
  "gate": "No unsourced amounts, medication advice, or hazardous equipment procedures; review relevant local official guidance. Do not ask viewers to guess an emergency response or choose an action in a simulated emergency; any response content must come from reviewed official guidance.",
